-- Newsroom drafts for 2026-11-18 (Wednesday). Loaded once into EDITORIAL_REVIEW; an editor approves before anything is published.
-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package or open draft (grepped content/, seed/ and the newsroom branches).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons could not be opened from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Wikimedia Commons thumbnails built from file names confirmed by search (MD5 path). Six are U.S. government works (White House, Senate, House, Defense Department, Air Force); three carry a Commons free license that the editor should confirm. The image check falls back to 800px or the original file if a thumbnail size is missing.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261118-trump-shenzhen-xi-tarmac', 'xi-greets-trump-tarmac-shenzhen-apec-manila-trade-understanding', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Xi greets Trump on the tarmac in Shenzhen as the president arrives for APEC after announcing a trade understanding in Manila', 'Trump landed in China on Wednesday, Nov. 18, local time, ahead of a planned three-way meeting with Xi Jinping and Vladimir Putin on Thursday, Nov. 19. In Manila, he and President Marcos announced an economic understanding whose terms were not released.', 'Chinese President Xi Jinping met President Trump at the foot of the aircraft stairs at Shenzhen Bao''an International Airport on Wednesday, Nov. 18, local time, as Trump arrived for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit, Ukrainian outlet UNN reported, citing CNN. CNN reported that Xi had never before greeted a U.S. president at an airport as head of state. Under recent Chinese protocol, leaders generally do not meet visitors on the tarmac.

## A ceremony with anthems and a flyover

The welcome included a handshake and an embrace, the playing of both national anthems and a flight display by the Chinese air force, according to a Time News roundup of regional reporting. Xi said he wanted to return the gesture after Trump greeted him at Joint Base Andrews earlier in 2026, UNN reported.

Putin also arrived in Shenzhen on Wednesday, Nov. 18, and was met by Cai Qi, a member of the Politburo Standing Committee. Xi and Putin held talks the same day, according to both reports.

## The three-way meeting

Trump, Xi and Putin are scheduled to meet on Thursday, Nov. 19, at the Qilin Villa, a state guesthouse about 30 minutes from the main APEC venue, Time News reported, citing the BBC. The Financial Times reported that the three governments had not agreed on an agenda, according to UNN. The Wall Street Journal reported that Putin wants to discuss ending the war in Ukraine on terms favorable to Moscow, while Trump mainly wants to talk about nuclear weapons.

Ukraine''s foreign minister, Andrii Sybiha, criticized the invitation to Putin, and President Volodymyr Zelenskyy said Ukraine should be consulted if the war is discussed, UNN reported.

## What came out of Manila

Before leaving the Philippines, Trump held talks with President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. at Malacañang Palace on Wednesday, Nov. 18, and called the result the biggest trade deal the two countries had ever made, the Daily Tribune of Manila reported. The palace described it as an understanding on economic cooperation, focused on energy and food security, rather than a finished trade agreement.

Neither government released a dollar value, terms or a timetable, the Tribune reported, and neither said whether the 12.5% additional tariffs the United States placed on some Philippine goods in July would change. Marcos also left for Shenzhen to attend APEC.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_(54890669668).jpg/1280px-President_Donald_Trump_greets_Chinese_President_Xi_Jinping_before_a_bilateral_meeting_at_the_Gimhae_International_Airport_terminal_(54890669668).jpg', 'President Trump greets Chinese President Xi Jinping at Gimhae International Airport in Busan, South Korea, in October 2025 (file). Official White House photo via Wikimedia Commons, public domain', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-18.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-18T10:55:00.000Z', '2026-11-18T10:55:00.000Z');
